  "query_preview": "..\nThe Marianas are situated on the northwest periphery of a broad, weak\ncirculation, Invest 98W, centered between Satawal and Chuuk Lagoon\nnear 8N150E. A trade-wind trough extends northward from Invest 98W,\nwith numerous showers and isolated thunderstorms seen along the axis,\napproaching the islands from the east. Scattered showers and \nisolated thunderstorms are expected tonight as the trade-wind trough\nshifts westward into the area, supported in part by divergence aloft\nassociated with an upper-level low and trough. Over the next few\ndays, model guidance shows most of the showers and thunderstorms \ndeveloping near Tinian and Saipan where the strongest convergence\nlooks to set up, as Invest 98W slowly meanders westward south of the\nislands, and an attendant trough to its northeast moves through the\narea. Late this weekend into early next week, a quieter ridging \npattern looks to move in behind 98W.",
